Description: Voice-to-text system for GNOME with OpenAI Whisper integration
 Voicetyping is a GNOME Shell extension with a Python backend that provides
 voice-to-text functionality using OpenAI Whisper or Groq APIs.
 .
 Features:
  - Real-time audio recording with keyboard shortcuts
  - Transcription via OpenAI Whisper or Groq
  - Automatic text insertion via virtual keyboard
  - Two-service architecture for privilege separation
  - GNOME Shell 47+ integration with panel indicator
 .
 The system uses two systemd services: voicetyping-core (user service) for
 audio recording and transcription, and voicetyping-keyboard (system service)
 for secure keyboard simulation via /dev/uinput.
